# promise: #819
# A double click on the sidebar's edge did nothing. In the reporter's Arc recording it puts the edge at Arc's
# default width, 228 pt, the width a drag snaps to (SidebarResize.doubleClickWidth), from a narrow sidebar and from
# a wide one alike. The two presses go to the edge as AppKit sends them (clickCount 1, then 2), and the width is
# kept for the next launch.
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=edge
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?sidebarEdge=doubleClick
wait 1
expect-log sidebar edge before: 328 pt
expect-log sidebar edge double click: 228 pt
expect-log sidebar edge after: 228 pt, saved 228 pt
